From 6c25924b481a862f5d08adb6b5e67f8b134a6d93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Victor C." <34163765+vicajilau@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 07:28:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gstpipewiresrc: fix NULL gst_buffer_unref() on first buffer
 with keepalive-time

gst_pipewire_src_create() unconditionally unrefs the previous
last_buffer when replacing it, without checking whether it's NULL.
On the very first buffer received with keepalive-time > 0 (or
resend-last=true), last_buffer is still NULL (never yet set), so
this becomes gst_buffer_unref(NULL), tripping the assertion inside
gst_mini_object_unref().

Regressed in e6a5951a4 ("gst: fix compilation on older GStreamer"),
which replaced the NULL-safe gst_buffer_take() with a manual
old/new swap that dropped the NULL check gst_buffer_take() provided
internally.

Fixes: e6a5951a4 ("gst: fix compilation on older GStreamer")

diff --git a/src/gst/gstpipewiresrc.c b/src/gst/gstpipewiresrc.c
index dbb5f289a..414a9ae08 100644
--- a/src/gst/gstpipewiresrc.c
+++ b/src/gst/gstpipewiresrc.c
@@ -1630,7 +1630,8 @@ gst_pipewire_src_create (GstPushSrc * psrc, GstBuffer ** buffer)
 
           old = pwsrc->last_buffer;
           pwsrc->last_buffer = gst_buffer_copy (buf);
-          gst_buffer_unref (old);
+          if (old != NULL)
+            gst_buffer_unref (old);
           gst_buffer_add_parent_buffer_meta (pwsrc->last_buffer, buf);
 
           clock = gst_element_get_clock (GST_ELEMENT_CAST (pwsrc));

